---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="AI-powered RFP & Proposal Pipeline">
<main class="case">
  <div class="case-hero shell">
    <a class="case-back" href="/work">← All work</a>
    <div class="eyebrow">Selected Work · AI & Automation</div>
    <h1>AI-powered RFP &amp; Proposal Pipeline</h1>
    <p class="case-lead">An end-to-end workflow for identifying, assessing and responding to donor-funded opportunities.</p>
    <div class="case-meta"><span>Role</span><strong>Programme / technology leadership</strong><span>Context</span><strong>Digital health</strong></div>
  </div>
  <section class="shell case-grid">
    <article>
      <div class="eyebrow">The challenge</div>
      <h2>Turn fragmented opportunity information into a usable pipeline.</h2>
      <p>The work brings opportunity ingestion, categorisation, partner matching, bid/no-bid assessment and proposal preparation into a connected workflow. The objective is not simply to generate text with AI, but to make the surrounding decision process more structured and repeatable.</p>
    </article>
    <aside class="case-panel">
      <div class="eyebrow">Workflow</div>
      <div class="step"><b>01</b> Opportunity ingestion</div>
      <div class="step"><b>02</b> AI categorisation</div>
      <div class="step"><b>03</b> Partner matching</div>
      <div class="step"><b>04</b> Bid / no-bid scoring</div>
      <div class="step"><b>05</b> Proposal generation</div>
    </aside>
  </section>
  <section class="shell case-grid reverse">
    <article>
      <div class="eyebrow">Approach</div>
      <h2>AI as workflow infrastructure, not a standalone chatbot.</h2>
      <p>The pipeline connects structured data, classification and decision support with the human work of assessing opportunities and building proposals. This reflects a practical approach to AI: automate repetitive processing while retaining human judgement where context and accountability matter.</p>
      <div class="tags"><span>AI</span><span>Automation</span><span>RFPs</span><span>Digital Health</span></div>
    </article>
    <aside class="case-note"><strong>What this demonstrates</strong><p>Process design · AI workflow integration · programme operations · proposal strategy · practical automation</p></aside>
  </section>
  <section class="case-dark"><div class="shell"><div class="eyebrow">Evidence</div><h2>From opportunity discovery to a decision-ready pipeline.</h2><p>The current CV describes this as an end-to-end automated pipeline spanning ingestion, categorisation, partner matching, storage, bid/no-bid scoring and proposal generation. This case study deliberately does not claim quantitative outcomes that are not documented in the source material.</p></div></section>
  <div class="shell case-next"><div class="eyebrow">Next</div><a href="/work/jembi">Jembi Health Systems →</a></div>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
